\measuredangle XKA=\measuredangle XCA 
=\measuredangle ZCP 
=\measuredangle KPC-\measuredangle KZC 
=\measuredangle KBA-\measuredangle KYX $$  We get  $\measuredangle (\ell,KX)=\measuredangle KYX$ , so  $\ell$  is tangent to  $(KYX)$ . This way we have proven that circles  $(ABP)$ ,  $(XYZ)$  are both tangent at  $K$  and the common tangent line is  $\ell$ .

