We shall show that \(QPFA\) is cyclic, whence by phantom point we would obtain that \(AC\), \(FD\) and \(BP\) concur.
Notice that 
\[\angle PQF = 180 - \angle PBD - \angle FDB = 180 - (180 - 2\gamma) - \alpha = 2\gamma - \alpha\]
We also have 
\[\angle PAF = \angle PAB = 180 - \angle APB - \angle ABP = \gamma - \angle FDP = 2\gamma - \alpha\]
Thus by phantom point we must have \(C-A-Q\), now it suffices to show that \(AC\) and \(DP\) are parallel, but this is obvious.

